description:
Design a circuit that determines the minimum value among four 32-bit unsigned inputs (a, b, c, and d). The module continuously evaluates the inputs and assigns the smallest value to the output `min`.
module top_module(
  input [31:0] a, b, c, d,
  output reg [31:0] min
);

code:
module top_module(
  input [31:0] a, b, c, d,
  output reg [31:0] min
);always @(*) begin
    if(a < b && a < c && a < d)
      min = a;
    else if(b < c && b < d)
      min = b;
    else if(c < d)
      min = c;
    else
      min = d;
  end

endmodule

