description:
Design a delay line circuit that introduces a delay of 'd' clock cycles to an input signal. The module consists of a shift register with 'd' stages, where the input signal is shifted through the register on each rising edge of the clock. The output is taken from the last stage of the shift register, effectively providing a delayed version of the input signal by 'd' clock cycles.
module top_module(
  input clk,
  input in,
  output out
);

code:
module top_module(
  input clk,
  input in,
  output out
);parameter d = 4; // number of clock cycles of delay

// Define a shift register with d stages
reg [d-1:0] sr;

always @(posedge clk) begin
  // Shift the input signal into the shift register
  sr <= {sr[d-2:0], in};
end

// Output the delayed signal from the d-th flip-flop
assign out = sr[d-1];

endmodule

