description:
Design a four-bit decoder that produces a 2-bit output based on the 4-bit input. The output is determined by specific ranges of the input: when the input is between 5 (inclusive) and 9 (exclusive), the output is set to 01; when the input is between 9 (inclusive) and 12 (exclusive), the output is 10; for all other inputs, it defaults to 11. This decoder effectively categorizes the 4-bit input into three distinct output states while ignoring the values outside the defined ranges.
module top_module(
    input [3:0] in,
    output reg [1:0] out
);

code:
module top_module(
    input [3:0] in,
    output reg [1:0] out
);always @*
begin
    case(in)
        4'b0000 : out = 2'b00;
        4'b0001 : out = 2'b00;
        4'b0010 : out = 2'b00;
        4'b0011 : out = 2'b00;
        4'b0100 : out = 2'b00;
        4'b0101 : out = 2'b01;
        4'b0110 : out = 2'b01;
        4'b0111 : out = 2'b01;
        4'b1000 : out = 2'b01;
        4'b1001 : out = 2'b10;
        4'b1010 : out = 2'b10;
        4'b1011 : out = 2'b10;
        default : out = 2'b11;
    endcase
end

endmodule

