description:
Design a crystal oscillator circuit that generates a clock signal with a specified frequency. The oscillator outputs a clock signal (clk) which toggles its state at half the specified frequency. A 32-bit counter is used to track the number of cycles, and the clk signal changes state when the counter reaches a value corresponding to half the desired frequency, effectively producing a square wave output at the specified frequency.
